{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791195705,"nonce":"sdATGYZCKCKfz7Sx8YHYkBaD3BY=","title":"Carets and text width: use Blinc's layout_with_fallbacks once it is pushed","message":"Blinc 941b2142 (not pushed yet as of 2026-10-05) adds `TextLayoutEngine::layout_with_fallbacks(text, font, size, options, \u0026faces)` with `FallbackFaces::resolve(\u0026mut registry, \u0026primary, text)`. It substitutes the fallback face's glyph and advance right after shaping, by the renderer's own rules, and each PositionedGlyph carries its `face`.\n\nToday blinc_abi's caret native (hl_blinc_text_carets) uses plain `layout`. So with any primary face whose missing-glyph advance differs from the fallback's, carets drift from what is drawn. blinc-b1 measured +6.37px per emoji under monospace and +3.55px under serif. Under SF Pro, U+2605 is off by -6.25px, because the primary has the glyph but the renderer treats it as emoji.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Bump Blinc to 941b2142 or later.\n- Switch hl_blinc_text_carets, and any other native that measures by `layout` (the measure context, canvas outlines), to `layout_with_fallbacks` with `FallbackFaces::resolve`.\n- Canvas outlines should take each glyph's outline from its own `face`.\n\n**Test:** a caret after \"a😀b\" and after \"★\" under monospace, serif and system, against the drawn glyph positions.\n\nBlinc's tracker: 124ad5d. Same Blinc commit: f3e4e62, repeated emoji (\"a😀😀b\") were drawn as one.","files":null}]}